    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nI've recently replaced vim-unimpaired with mini-bracketed but I'm missing these mappings which  I think are very useful:\n\n> *>p*    Paste after linewise, increasing indent.\n> *>P*    Paste before linewise, increasing indent.\n> *<p*    Paste after linewise, decreasing indent.\n> *<P*    Paste before linewise, decreasing indent.\n> *=p*    Paste after linewise, reindenting.\n> *=P*    Paste before linewise, reindenting.\n\nI understand these are not \"bracketed\" commands, but still immensely useful",
