        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThis is indeed outside of 'mini.bracketed' scope. It is more oriented towards targets that can be thought about as \"next\" / \"previous\" / \"first\" / \"last\" and not \"before\" / \"after\".\n\nThe one useful pair of mappings (in my opinion) here is to put before/after linewise with reindent. MiniMax contains [custom mappings](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/a7820cdb1e8e1bac796759323a1da3beae28415a/configs/nvim-0.11/plugin/20_keymaps.lua#L12-L20) for that. The reindent is only possible on Neovim>=0.12 by using `:iput[!]` instead of `:put[!]`.",
