        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Thanks for linking to the custom mappings, would there be some kind of simple workaround for =/</>p (compatible with <0.12)?\n\nNot that I'd call \"simple and robust\". It is possible to append `>>^` and `<<^` afterwards to indent/dedent and go to first non-blank. But it will probably not work as intended for already indented lines. Here are the mappings:\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set('n', '>P', '<Cmd>exe \"put! \" . v:register<CR>>>^', { desc = 'Paste Above and Indent' })\nvim.keymap.set('n', '>p', '<Cmd>exe \"put \"  . v:register<CR>>>^', { desc = 'Paste Below and Indent' })\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<P', '<Cmd>exe \"put! \" . v:register<CR><<^', { desc = 'Paste Above and Dedent' })\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<p', '<Cmd>exe \"put \"  . v:register<CR><<^', { desc = 'Paste Below and Dedent' })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-11-18T09:44:47Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2119#issuecomment-3546515706",
            "id": 3546515706,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2119",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOFoksYM7TY4j6",
